namespace FlexFlow {
/**

@page compile-model compile-model

\brief Run the model specified by the mapped PCG, encoded as JSON.

The main entry point for the %FlexFlow %Train compiler. The compiler takes a computation graph describing the operations to be performed, an transforms it into a mapped parallel computation graph (PCG) that describes how to do so on a parallel machine.

\verbatim
$ proj cmake # if you haven't already
...
$ proj build
...
$ ./build/normal/bin/compile-model/compile-model -h
\endverbatim

The above should print the help message for `compile-model`.

A typical workflow would involve generating a model (e.g., via \ref export-model-arch), compiling it, and then running (via \ref run-model):

\verbatim
$ ./build/normal/bin/export-model-arch/export-model-arch split_test > split_test_cg.json
$ ./build/normal/bin/compile-model/compile-model split_test_cg.json split_test_mpcg.json passthrough
$ ./build/normal/bin/run-model/run-model split_test_mpcg.json
\endverbatim

*/
}
